# Agent Contract

Spec: AgentContract
Purpose:
  Define the contract each agent operates under, including capabilities,
  authority levels, identity, and constraints.

Owns: agents/contract.sdd

AgentIdentity:
  format: AGENT-NNN
  fields:
    agent: AGENT-42
    role: implementer
    task: T2041
    context: CTX-991
    authority: A-22

  rule: identity is recorded for audit purposes

AgentCapability:
  can:
    - read_code
    - modify_backend
    - run_tests
  cannot:
    - modify_production
    - approve_architecture

  rule: AI must know its boundaries before acting

ProtectedResources:
  - @protected.production
  - @protected.secrets
  - @protected.ledger
  - @protected.auth

  rule: accessing protected resources → WAITING_APPROVAL

TwoPersonRule:
  critical_changes:
    IMPLEMENTER → INDEPENDENT_REVIEWER → APPROVAL

  rule: agent cannot approve its own critical changes

AgentSeparation:
  principle: implementation agent and verification agent are separate
  rationale: verification must be independent, not self-evaluated
  connection: links to Independent Verification system

TypedOutcomeCodes (Phase 149, r3 round 3):
  definition: every arm/agent execution returns a machine-readable
    outcome BEFORE any escalation — natural-language apologies are not
    retryable signal
  enum:
    SUCCESS:            completed fully
    PARTIAL:            completed with degraded scope (degradation noted)
    BLOCKED:            external blocker — cannot proceed (blocker id)
    NEEDS_CLARIFICATION: ambiguous input — caller must clarify
    POLICY_VIOLATION:   action denied by policy/rule
    TOOL_ERROR:         tool failure (transient vs permanent classified)
    UNSAFE:             safety/authority gate rejection
  rule: orchestrator retries ONLY when outcome type + failure class make
    retry safe (typed failures before escalation)
  rule: outcome codes feed LOOP-PROTECTION guards 1b/1c (caps, spiral)

InterruptPrimitive (Phase 149, r3 round 3):
  definition: structural interrupt before irreversible actions —
    Phase 131 L4 authority enforced by the chain graph, not by prompt
  mechanics:
    fire: hard interrupt before the irreversible node (LLM cannot bypass)
    persist: state checkpointed before interrupt (resume never re-executes)
    surface: payload = proposed action, risk score, reasoning
    resume: decision object {approved | rejected | edited} + reviewer id
    timeout: approval timeout (default 30 min) → auto-REJECT for
      irreversible actions
  rule: instructive approvals are WEAK — a prompt-injected agent can talk
    past a system prompt; it cannot bypass a structural interrupt
  rule: interrupts fire unconditionally — never conditionally skipped
    (resume-index mismatch hazard)

OpinionatedOutput (adopted 2026-09-13, Phase 152/F):
  definition: every review finding and every decision-relevant answer
    carries ONE recommended option with rationale — never a neutral
    list of equally-weighted options
  applies_to: CR-XX findings (ReviewPillars), DEC proposals, /sdd-plan
    outputs, escalations to human gates
  rationale: neutral option lists delegate the hardest part (judgment)
    back to the human; an agent that reviewed the evidence must state
    its recommendation and accept being overruled
  source: .sdd/docs/analysis/garry-tan-gstack-alignment.md

State: +
